  "conclusion": "C1 design boundary (noise floor 0.15 pp; plain-SA offset 9.21 mV = 0.39 V_T, run_offset_mc N=120): with slope-matched max-gain readout, the plain StrongARM SA is Pareto-optimal for MNIST-scale fan-in at V_in>=0.5 V (its 0.39 V_T lands at sigma_pc~2-4, below the curve knee -> drop within the 0.15 pp single-run MNIST noise, so auto-zero/chopping only ADD area+energy for no SIGNIFICANT accuracy). Offset cancellation earns its cost ONLY in the low-V_in (<=0.4 V) / wide-fan-in (F=1024) / under-budgeted-gain corner (layer2@0.4V: plain drop 0.24 pp, auto-zero recovers +0.11 pp). => Spec-inverted result: budget offset against V_T, not TMR margin, and skip auto-zero unless the readout gain budget forces it. Closes errata R2 as a quantified boundary, not 'auto-zero mandatory'. (Firming sigma 11.05->9.21 mV widened the plain-SA-sufficient region.)"
